  "captions": [
    "Stater: Barley (obverse); Barley, Incuse (reverse) c. 530–510 BCE · silver In Skald: Book 2, line 290 — after Athena tells Telemachus to pack barley meal. Metapontion, a Greek city in South Italy, stamped its barley on this coin long after the poem. Cleveland Museum of Art",
    "Tetradrachm (Coin) Depicting the God Dionysos Greek; minted in Maroneia, Thrace · mid–2nd century BCE In Skald: Book 9, line 197 — after Maron’s gift of wine. Maroneia, said to be named after him, put Dionysos, the god of wine, on its silver centuries later. The Art Institute of Chicago"
